<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Asopus (Boeotia)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Asopus is a river of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boeotia">Boeotia</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, which rises near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-cithaeron">Mount Cithaeron</a> and flows east past the territories of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-plataea">Plataea</a> and Tanagra to the Euboean Gulf. In 479 BCE the Greek and Persian armies faced each other across it for days before the Battle of Plataea. Its valley formed part of the border zone between Boeotia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attica">Attica</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/asopus-boeotia.jpg" alt="Asopus (Boeotia)" width="320" height="181" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Geraki · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plataea_battlefield.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
